@startuml poll-verify
' cumin works - the way out of cumin/status/implementing: the decision at the end of an Implementer run and at every poll.
' Document: poll.md, sections on the end of a run and the way back to the Owner.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

start
:The Implementer run ends, or a poll finds an issue in
cumin/status/implementing with no Implementer running;
if (The run returned blocked?) then (yes)
  :Post blocked_reason on the issue,
  change the label to cumin/status/awaiting-decision,
  and notify the Owner;
  stop
else (no: done, abnormal end, or no run in this cumin)
endif
:Read the issue again (one issue);
:Read who added cumin/status/implementing, and when;
:Read the decision requests after the label,
the open pull requests of the branch (REST),
the head commit of the worktree, and the state file;
if (A read failed, or the label is not
of cumin-core or of an Owner?) then (yes)
  :Change nothing.
  The next poll decides from the same facts;
  stop
else (no)
endif
partition "Decision (pure function ImplementationEnd, no I/O)" {
  if (A decision request after the label?) then (yes)
    :stop the implementation for the Owner
    (the question is the reason);
  elseif (The pull request passes the check?
  (on the branch, by the Implementer App, head pushed)) then (yes)
    if (The request was a conflict resolution, and
    the head commit is older than the label?) then (yes)
      :stop the implementation for the Owner
      (the conflict is not resolved);
    else (no)
      :wait for the checks;
    endif
  elseif (Requested again during this stay?
  (count in the state file)) then (yes)
    :stop the implementation for the Owner
    (the failed check, retried once);
  else (no)
    :request the implementation again;
  endif
}
note right
  wait for the checks: cumin-core adds the closing link
  when it is missing, then cumin/status/checking.
  stop: the label changes to cumin/status/awaiting-decision
  first, then the comment (not for a question), then the
  notification.
  request again: the quota decides, the count rises, and the
  Implementer runs in the kept session. Its end comes back
  to the top of this diagram.
end note
stop
@enduml
